    "provinceDeepAtlasProfile": {
      "oneLine": "El'dravire Riverrealm is centered at -16.033105, 61.118515 under Parliamentary Government, with 133,430,000 people across 12 settlements.",
      "extremeAtlasDescription": "El'dravire Riverrealm occupies 6,815,430.47 sq mi / 17,651,883.88 sq km of modeled Earth-sized territory, about 3.460707% of Belavadös's surface. It is not merely a province but a continent-scale civic machine: Beach and grass with water, Partial forest and Beach and reefs with water define its broad terrain, while its settlements intensify into Beach and grass with water, Farming, Marshes and swamps, Beach and reefs with water and Ocean Surface floating settlement. Population density is 7.559 people/sq km / 19.578 people/sq mi, which lets wilderness, roads, faction-held corridors, and vast uncrowded borders remain huge.",
      "peopleFactionsAndFaith": "The strongest public people-groups are Humans, Near-Humans, and Mixed Heritage, Halfling and Smallfolk, Animalfolk and Mammalian Anthropomorphs, Elf Parent Race and Elf Bloodlines, Amphibious and Aquatic Peoples, Fey and Trickster Folk, and 2 more. Frequently recorded peoples include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Harengon, Elf — Wood Elf, Elf — Eladrin, Fey-Folk — Faerie, Satyr, Changeling, and 4 more. Faction visibility leans toward The Black-Maw Myriad, with worship and patronage records naming Nebyrr, Ishtanora, Iskareth, Thoryn-Rahek, Bastveig, Sigrananna, Hathruna, and 3 more.",
      "groupLinkDescription": "The province participates in 6 recorded four-province geography group links, including 5 cross-transportation-group links. These links place it inside overlapping regional corridors rather than one isolated block, allowing border-adjacent transit, faction influence, and cultural spillover to breathe across group lines.",
